WEBVTT

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:40.016
I've been observing your matches.

00:01:40.392 --> 00:01:43.978
You're all much stronger than I would
expect of middle schoolers.

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:48.692
But strengthening your mental ability

00:01:48.692 --> 00:01:50.610
will make you even better.

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:52.112
Mental ability.

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:55.365
First, pair up.

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:57.534
Anyone's fine.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:03.289
You will now play singles matches.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.458
What? Singles?

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:08.878
Those who lose will drop out.

00:02:10.005 --> 00:02:13.800
You will play against the
partners you grouped with.

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:20.390
"Friendly Fire"

00:02:24.686 --> 00:02:28.023
We're supposed to play
against our own allies,

00:02:28.023 --> 00:02:31.443
and force our chosen
partners to drop out?

00:02:34.029 --> 00:02:36.239
I can't believe this is what he meant

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:37.782
by strengthening our mental ability.

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:40.702
This is ridiculous! I can't do this!

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:44.372
Let's begin with pairs from here to here.

00:02:44.372 --> 00:02:46.833
Hey, are you even listening,
you lanky bastard?

00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:48.626
Oh, and...

00:02:48.918 --> 00:02:53.048
...pairs who don't comply will
also be eliminated, yes.

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:58.470
Probability of avoiding these matches: 0%.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.388
In order to survive...

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.807
We have to play.

00:03:03.058 --> 00:03:04.267
Bastard.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.102
Um...

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:09.147
You'll play according to
tiebreaker rules, all right?

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:12.108
Okay, it's time to begin.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.069
Uh, oh...

00:03:14.444 --> 00:03:16.446
What's gonna happen?

00:03:24.788 --> 00:03:27.248
Are we really going to do this?

00:03:33.296 --> 00:03:34.798
Shishido-<i>san</i>, I...

00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:40.804
Don't just stand there, Chotaro!

00:03:40.804 --> 00:03:42.931
The match has already begun!

00:03:43.848 --> 00:03:45.350
Shishido-<i>san</i>...

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.436
It's your serve.

00:03:48.436 --> 00:03:50.772
Give me your best Scud Serve.

00:04:06.162 --> 00:04:07.330
Here we go.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.206
Bring it on.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.127
Let's go, Yuushi.

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:15.338
Whoever loses, no hard feelings.

00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:17.924
I'm glad you said that.

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:20.802
I couldn't bear having you hate me.

00:04:21.177 --> 00:04:22.846
Shut up, Yuushi!

00:04:22.846 --> 00:04:24.806
You think it's a given that you'll win?

00:04:25.306 --> 00:04:26.975
Of course I do.

00:04:26.975 --> 00:04:30.812
No one steps onto the court
thinking he'll lose...

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.732
...no matter who he's up against.

00:04:34.149 --> 00:04:38.653
I'll win this match... You'll see!

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.995
Just so you know, Niou-<i>kun</i>,

00:04:46.995 --> 00:04:51.249
you should assume your tricks
won't work against me.

00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:53.251
What are you saying?

00:04:53.251 --> 00:04:57.255
I have absolutely no intention
of trying to trick you.

00:04:57.255 --> 00:04:59.174
Let's battle it out fair and square.

00:04:59.758 --> 00:05:01.968
Fair and square, you say?

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:07.098
You know I'm not stupid
enough to believe that.

00:05:30.955 --> 00:05:32.749
They've started.

00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:35.251
Are they really gonna play?

00:05:39.923 --> 00:05:42.092
Looks like they're starting over there, too.

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:44.511
That's Seigaku's...

00:05:44.761 --> 00:05:46.680
Seigaku? You don't mean...

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:49.516
After all this...

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.977
Why do those two have to
play against each other?

00:05:53.603 --> 00:05:56.106
Cool and collected Oishi-<i>senpai</i>...

00:05:56.106 --> 00:06:00.485
and the always acrobatic and
surprising Kikumaru-<i>senpai</i>.

00:06:00.777 --> 00:06:05.073
Seigaku's invincible doubles
team, the Golden Pair.

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:08.118
To make the two of them fight
against each other for survival...

00:06:08.118 --> 00:06:10.036
It's too much!

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.579
Over there!

00:06:13.498 --> 00:06:14.499
Yahoo!

00:06:14.499 --> 00:06:15.625
Kikumaru Beam!

00:06:17.252 --> 00:06:20.046
What is this?

00:06:20.588 --> 00:06:23.174
He doesn't seem sad... He seems...

00:06:23.717 --> 00:06:25.051
...to be having fun.

00:06:26.344 --> 00:06:28.638
Hey! Kikumaru Bazooka!

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:33.852
Oops. I messed up.

00:06:34.686 --> 00:06:36.271
What?

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:41.776
Doesn't Kikumaru-<i>senpai</i>
understand what's going on?

00:06:47.198 --> 00:06:49.576
How are they playing today?

00:06:49.576 --> 00:06:51.619
Now, then...

00:06:51.619 --> 00:06:54.330
Everything's going more or less as expected.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:57.459
Though, one of them refuses to cooperate.

00:07:01.463 --> 00:07:04.507
Here comes the next one!

00:07:07.469 --> 00:07:09.137
Now, then...

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:20.106
I got this one!

00:07:29.491 --> 00:07:31.785
That's quite the hit, Koshimae.

00:07:34.662 --> 00:07:37.207
You haven't forgotten our promise, have you?

00:07:37.791 --> 00:07:40.710
Tell me where I can find Court 1.

00:07:46.591 --> 00:07:48.426
I'm just guessing,

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:49.969
but I don't think he could

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:52.347
tell you even if he wanted to.

00:07:52.347 --> 00:07:54.307
Hey, middle schoolers.

00:07:55.433 --> 00:07:58.353
You've gone far enough.

00:08:01.606 --> 00:08:05.402
Koshimae, a whole slew of
challengers have appeared.

00:08:05.735 --> 00:08:07.112
This is getting interesting.

00:08:08.029 --> 00:08:09.823
Looks like we'll have some fun this time.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.409
Pathetic middle schoolers.

00:08:12.867 --> 00:08:15.995
Your arrogance won't last long.

00:08:19.958 --> 00:08:22.585
Boom! Kikumaru Bazooka!

00:08:24.379 --> 00:08:27.132
Kikumaru Jet Bazooka!

00:08:27.132 --> 00:08:28.800
Kikumaru-<i>senpai</i>...

00:08:29.259 --> 00:08:31.261
Something's not right.

00:08:31.511 --> 00:08:35.140
His reaction time and his
breathing are slightly off

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:38.268
from his normal numbers.

00:08:38.268 --> 00:08:41.021
What's up with Eiji?

00:08:41.021 --> 00:08:41.896
Hey!

00:08:42.355 --> 00:08:43.857
Kikumaru's not the only one.

00:08:43.857 --> 00:08:44.774
What?

00:08:46.901 --> 00:08:48.236
Are you sure?

00:08:51.156 --> 00:08:54.951
What's your decision, Oishi?

00:08:56.494 --> 00:08:57.370
Hey!

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.748
Kikumaru's Seal... Oops!

00:09:01.916 --> 00:09:04.544
Damn, I messed up again.

00:09:25.732 --> 00:09:27.150
Oishi?

00:09:35.367 --> 00:09:36.951
Not bad!

00:09:36.951 --> 00:09:38.995
I won't lose!

00:09:38.995 --> 00:09:40.622
Enough, Eiji!

00:09:42.165 --> 00:09:45.335
How long are you going to keep up the act?

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:46.753
What act?

00:09:46.753 --> 00:09:47.962
What does he mean?

00:09:48.755 --> 00:09:49.839
I see.

00:09:49.839 --> 00:09:52.550
Eiji must've been intentionally playing poorly

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:55.679
in order to prolong the match.

00:09:55.679 --> 00:09:56.638
What?

00:09:56.638 --> 00:10:02.602
He couldn't bear to fight against
the man he's played doubles with,

00:10:02.602 --> 00:10:04.604
knowing the loser will be eliminated.

00:10:05.146 --> 00:10:09.317
Oishi and Eiji have always been one.

00:10:10.652 --> 00:10:12.987
They're the only middle schoolers

00:10:12.987 --> 00:10:17.534
who've mastered the Synchronization
technique to unify their minds.

00:10:20.328 --> 00:10:23.164
What? You knew?

00:10:23.164 --> 00:10:24.082
Yeah.

00:10:24.082 --> 00:10:25.667
Oops.

00:10:25.667 --> 00:10:29.004
I guess I can't hide anything from you.

00:10:29.838 --> 00:10:33.174
I noticed it the moment I
received your first serve.

00:10:35.927 --> 00:10:38.722
It was almost too easy to
know what you were thinking.

00:10:39.597 --> 00:10:41.266
It was the worst...

00:10:42.726 --> 00:10:45.520
...Synchronization I've ever experienced.

00:10:47.605 --> 00:10:50.984
Then what're we supposed to do?

00:10:51.359 --> 00:10:55.905
If we finish this match,
one of us will have to drop out.

00:10:55.905 --> 00:10:57.198
Is that what you want?

00:10:57.699 --> 00:11:00.952
But what use is dragging out the match?

00:11:01.286 --> 00:11:02.787
Don't you get it?

00:11:02.787 --> 00:11:05.123
When one of us loses here...

00:11:05.457 --> 00:11:08.001
...I won't get to play doubles
with you anymore.

00:11:08.001 --> 00:11:10.045
When one of us loses?

00:11:11.212 --> 00:11:14.883
Sorry, but I won't be losing
to you as you are now.

00:11:15.633 --> 00:11:18.803
I will win this match.

00:11:19.095 --> 00:11:21.556
I will remain at this camp!

00:11:21.931 --> 00:11:23.725
I will not run!

00:11:37.781 --> 00:11:39.657
Six-one, Oishi!

00:11:40.575 --> 00:11:44.120
One more point and Oishi-<i>senpai </i>will win.

00:11:44.371 --> 00:11:47.499
I can't believe Kikumaru-<i>senpai </i>will...

00:11:52.671 --> 00:11:55.048
I-It's over!

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.892
I-It's over!

00:12:10.522 --> 00:12:13.108
Who are we, Eiji?

00:12:17.278 --> 00:12:19.823
The U-17 camp?

00:12:19.823 --> 00:12:23.118
Yeah, we've received a special invitation.

00:12:23.618 --> 00:12:26.162
Does that mean I'll get
to play doubles with you

00:12:26.162 --> 00:12:27.997
one more time before we graduate?

00:12:28.456 --> 00:12:29.958
That's right.

00:12:31.209 --> 00:12:33.837
Yay! All right!

00:12:36.673 --> 00:12:39.342
I guess it'll be the very last time.

00:12:39.342 --> 00:12:39.843
What?

00:12:40.802 --> 00:12:45.265
It'll probably be the very
last time we play together.

00:12:50.395 --> 00:12:54.149
We'll have to part ways eventually...

00:12:55.734 --> 00:12:59.738
but no matter what happens,
we'll always be the Golden Pair.

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:01.698
No matter what.

00:13:02.866 --> 00:13:03.950
Oishi.

00:13:09.289 --> 00:13:12.792
Hey, now! I can't believe you
said that with a straight face!

00:13:14.044 --> 00:13:16.963
Don't laugh! Eiji!

00:13:19.924 --> 00:13:21.384
You're right.

00:13:23.553 --> 00:13:24.596
We're...

00:13:25.722 --> 00:13:26.890
We're...

00:13:33.938 --> 00:13:35.815
Six-two, Kikumaru!

00:13:36.232 --> 00:13:37.734
Kikumaru-<i>senpai</i>.

00:13:38.026 --> 00:13:40.528
Kikumaru's performing
at his usual numbers...

00:13:40.528 --> 00:13:42.655
No, better.

00:13:43.656 --> 00:13:45.241
No matter what happens...

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.411
Even if we're pitted against each other...

00:13:48.828 --> 00:13:50.246
We'll always give it our all.

00:13:51.373 --> 00:13:54.501
Yeah, that's what it really means...

00:13:54.501 --> 00:13:56.461
...to be the Golden Pair!

00:14:05.011 --> 00:14:06.721
Let's go, Eiji!

00:14:06.721 --> 00:14:08.014
All right!

00:14:08.014 --> 00:14:09.265
Bring it on, partner!

00:14:12.936 --> 00:14:14.604
What an intense rally.

00:14:14.604 --> 00:14:17.315
It's a completely different game now.

00:14:17.315 --> 00:14:21.069
This is the battle of Seigaku's Golden Pair.

00:14:23.321 --> 00:14:27.867
Kikumaru-<i>senpai </i>and Oishi-<i>senpai</i>
are fighting so fiercely.

00:14:28.326 --> 00:14:30.662
They've got their Synchronization.

00:14:31.079 --> 00:14:37.043
They both know exactly what
the other is thinking.

00:14:37.752 --> 00:14:42.340
What'll happen when the two
of them go head-to-head?

00:14:43.091 --> 00:14:46.344
If their special techniques won't
work against each other...

00:14:47.721 --> 00:14:49.848
It's a battle of brute force.

00:14:53.351 --> 00:14:56.354
I've never seen Oishi-<i>senpai</i>
or Kikumaru-<i>senpai</i>

00:14:56.354 --> 00:15:00.567
play tennis like this before, but it's...

00:15:00.567 --> 00:15:02.193
They seem to be having fun.

00:15:03.403 --> 00:15:04.612
Of course they are.

00:15:06.197 --> 00:15:09.576
They've fought through
countless battles together.

00:15:11.536 --> 00:15:14.372
Not only do they know each other's strength,

00:15:14.372 --> 00:15:16.458
but their abilities are also equal.

00:15:18.043 --> 00:15:19.127
Game and match!

00:15:19.127 --> 00:15:20.962
Oshitari! Seven-zero!

00:15:20.962 --> 00:15:23.340
Damn it, Yuushi!

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:25.300
You closed your mind!

00:15:25.842 --> 00:15:29.721
Forgive me, Gakuto.
Shame it had to come to this.

00:15:32.474 --> 00:15:34.559
Are you all right, Niou-<i>kun</i>?

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:38.563
Lay off, Yagyuu.

00:15:38.897 --> 00:15:40.982
I'll never lose to you.

00:15:41.941 --> 00:15:43.902
That's the spirit.

00:15:44.486 --> 00:15:46.905
But the battle is heartless.

00:15:47.697 --> 00:15:49.574
He won't be able to reach

00:15:49.574 --> 00:15:53.286
a Laser Beam to the right with that leg.

00:15:54.412 --> 00:15:55.997
Adieu, Niou-<i>kun</i>.

00:15:56.748 --> 00:16:00.168
This Laser will end the match!

00:16:03.046 --> 00:16:04.255
Gotcha.

00:16:06.132 --> 00:16:08.718
Is that fake blood?

00:16:09.052 --> 00:16:11.137
The injury was a trick.

00:16:12.681 --> 00:16:18.061
Niou-<i>kun</i>, how long have we
played doubles together?

00:16:20.689 --> 00:16:22.732
Game and match, Yagyuu!

00:16:22.732 --> 00:16:24.109
Eight-six!

00:16:25.318 --> 00:16:26.361
What?

00:16:27.153 --> 00:16:31.825
The tone of your voice drops
slightly when you use a trick.

00:16:32.367 --> 00:16:33.993
Haven't you noticed?

00:16:36.788 --> 00:16:38.707
Game and match, Otori!

00:16:38.707 --> 00:16:39.958
Nine-seven!

00:16:42.877 --> 00:16:44.629
Damn it!

00:16:45.422 --> 00:16:46.881
That was close.

00:16:46.881 --> 00:16:49.092
When you returned all my Scud Serves,

00:16:49.092 --> 00:16:50.552
I thought I was done for.

00:16:50.552 --> 00:16:52.637
Don't get ahead of yourself, Chotaro.

00:16:52.637 --> 00:16:55.557
There's plenty of guys who'll do that here.

00:16:55.849 --> 00:16:56.725
Okay.

00:16:59.644 --> 00:17:02.105
Hey, stick out your hand.

00:17:02.105 --> 00:17:03.064
What?

00:17:06.359 --> 00:17:09.446
Isn't that grip a little small for you?

00:17:12.657 --> 00:17:14.367
Take this grip tape.

00:17:15.118 --> 00:17:16.703
Go with confidence.

00:17:16.703 --> 00:17:18.288
You defeated me.

00:17:19.831 --> 00:17:22.208
Yes. Thank you.

00:17:22.709 --> 00:17:27.547
Don't make that face. You look kinda lame.

00:17:27.547 --> 00:17:28.590
Kinda lame?

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:29.841
Ahem...

00:17:30.717 --> 00:17:34.929
Shishido-<i>kun</i>, you're trying to
get people to say that now?

00:17:35.764 --> 00:17:36.848
I wasn't...

00:17:37.974 --> 00:17:38.767
Pupina.

00:17:39.267 --> 00:17:41.311
Niou-<i>kun</i>, you too?

00:17:41.728 --> 00:17:43.313
That'll never catch on.

00:17:43.313 --> 00:17:45.857
Niou, that's kinda lame.

00:17:45.857 --> 00:17:47.567
Enough, you two.

00:17:47.567 --> 00:17:48.485
Pupina.

00:17:48.485 --> 00:17:50.153
Come on.

00:17:50.153 --> 00:17:50.695
Pupina.

00:17:50.695 --> 00:17:52.113
That's kinda lame.

00:17:52.113 --> 00:17:56.076
A draining match between
equally matched players.

00:17:56.534 --> 00:17:59.287
What a good use of time.

00:17:59.829 --> 00:18:01.998
They're all sporting good expressions.

00:18:02.749 --> 00:18:09.005
But that doesn't change the fact
that their friends are eliminated.

00:18:29.526 --> 00:18:32.362
It's over, Oishi.

00:18:34.239 --> 00:18:37.867
So it seems, unfortunately.

00:18:40.412 --> 00:18:44.124
But even if we're apart...

00:18:44.708 --> 00:18:46.501
We'll still be the Golden Pair.

00:18:48.503 --> 00:18:50.255
Game and match, Kikumaru!

00:18:50.255 --> 00:18:51.548
Eight-six!

00:19:06.438 --> 00:19:08.481
Leave your racquet.

00:19:12.986 --> 00:19:17.323
I'll become an U-17
representative with it.

00:19:19.659 --> 00:19:21.995
I'm counting on you, Eiji.

00:19:24.039 --> 00:19:25.206
Course!

00:19:31.212 --> 00:19:34.257
These matches are rough.

00:19:34.507 --> 00:19:37.010
Did you think it would be easy, Kawamura?

00:19:37.844 --> 00:19:39.429
We didn't come here to fool around.

00:19:40.722 --> 00:19:41.890
Akutsu.

00:19:43.808 --> 00:19:48.271
How are the rest of the matches
gonna go after a start like that?

00:19:48.813 --> 00:19:51.941
Atobe Hyotei-<i>san </i>against Hiyoshi-<i>san</i>.

00:19:52.776 --> 00:19:55.445
Captain Tezuka and Kaidoh-<i>senpai</i>.

00:19:56.404 --> 00:20:01.076
Wow. All of these matches are amazing.

00:20:10.418 --> 00:20:13.171
Ah, that was fun.

00:20:13.171 --> 00:20:15.715
They've got even stronger
guys in their base.

00:20:15.715 --> 00:20:17.884
Isn't this exciting, Koshimae?

00:20:17.884 --> 00:20:19.427
Their base?

00:20:19.427 --> 00:20:21.096
You mean Court 1?

00:20:21.388 --> 00:20:24.516
I wonder how strong the next guys will be.

00:20:25.475 --> 00:20:28.353
I wish you'd leave me alone already.

00:20:30.689 --> 00:20:32.190
What's up?

00:20:32.649 --> 00:20:34.150
I found their base.

00:20:34.943 --> 00:20:36.528
That's...

00:20:37.237 --> 00:20:39.572
Oh, it's that Oni guy.

00:20:39.572 --> 00:20:42.158
Maybe he knows where Court 1 is.

00:20:44.452 --> 00:20:47.914
He's got a lot of balls.

00:20:58.425 --> 00:21:00.468
Court 1's Tokugawa!

00:21:05.348 --> 00:21:07.308
Check it out, Koshimae.

00:21:07.767 --> 00:21:09.853
They're rallying with five balls.

00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:14.107
What do you wanna do?

00:21:14.107 --> 00:21:15.150
You wanna go?

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:17.569
We're gonna go, right, Koshimae?

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:22.198
Of course we are. That's why we're here.

